Title: The Long Way Home
Credit: Written by
Author: A Screenwriter
Draft date: 2026-05-23
Contact: writer@example.com

FADE IN:

INT. DINER - NIGHT

Rain whips the windows. A single fluorescent tube hums overhead. The place is empty except for one booth.

ELLA, 30s, picks at a slice of pie she hasn't eaten. Across from her: DANNY, late 30s, his coat still on, still wet.

ELLA
How long have you been driving?

DANNY
Since Tuesday.

ELLA
(quietly)
Danny.

DANNY
I know.

A long beat. Ella sets her fork down.

ELLA
You can't just show up.

DANNY
I didn't know where else to go.

= Ella decides whether to let him stay. She lets him stay.

CUT TO:

EXT. PARKING LOT - LATER

They walk together to her car. Neither speaks. The rain has stopped.

DANNY (CONT'D)
You kept the Volvo.

ELLA
It runs.

She unlocks the door. Looks at him.

ELLA (CONT'D)
Get in.

FADE OUT.

THE END
